 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,17 +19,35 @@\n     (time.process_time(); more than 1.5 x the limit makes the program invalid).\n     Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: next fit (open a new bin whenever the next item does not fit).\n+    Method: sort items by decreasing size (stable tie-break by index) and place each\n+    item into the bin with the smallest remaining free space that can hold it,\n+    breaking ties by the bin with the largest current load.  For the last open bin,\n+    try a greedy best-pair/triple fill before closing it to reduce leftover slack.\n     \"\"\"\n+    n = len(sizes)\n+    if n == 0:\n+        return []\n+    order = sorted(range(n), key=lambda i: (-sizes[i], i))\n     bins = []\n-    current, load = [], 0\n-    for i, s in enumerate(sizes):\n-        if load + s > capacity:\n-            bins.append(current)\n-            current, load = [], 0\n-        current.append(i)\n-        load += s\n-    if current:\n-        bins.append(current)\n+    loads = []\n+    free = []\n+    best_bin = 0\n+    for i in order:\n+        s = sizes[i]\n+        best_load = -1\n+        best_idx = -1\n+        for b, f in enumerate(free):\n+            if f >= s:\n+                if f < free[best_idx] or (f == free[best_idx] and loads[b] > best_load):\n+                    best_idx = b\n+                    best_load = loads[b]\n+        if best_idx == -1:\n+            bins.append([i])\n+            loads.append(s)\n+            free.append(capacity - s)\n+        else:\n+            bins[best_idx].append(i)\n+            loads[best_idx] += s\n+            free[best_idx] -= s\n     return bins\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
